digraph {
	77 [label="MarieRank1Convo3 begins.",color=orange];
		77 -> 78;
	78 [label="Il y a un crâne volant ! Keksekça ?! There is a flying talking skull and everyone is going on about their days as if nothing is happening and I need someone to acknowledge the strangeness of their whole existence.",shape=box,color=blue];
		78 -> 79;
		78 -> 81;
		78 -> 80;
	79 [label="That's just Necraloid. Well, a necraloid. It's complicated.",shape=box,color=red];
		79 -> 82;
	81 [label="That is Necraloid. He's a Cephalon, he won't hurt you.",shape=box,color=red];
		81 -> 84;
	80 [label="[End.]",shape=box,color=red];
		80 -> 83;
	82 [label="Pardon, is it a name or an object ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		82 -> 85;
		82 -> 86;
	84 [label="I do not think him a threat ! He does not frighten me.",shape=box,color=blue];
		84 -> 87;
	83 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	85 [label="I... don't rightly know.",shape=box,color=red];
		85 -> 88;
	86 [label="Yes.",shape=box,color=red];
		86 -> 89;
	87 [label="Indeed, I find him perfectly charming, if a bit unyielding in conversation. Not wholly unlike his living inspiration. But given the nature of my favored traveling companion, you can tell that does not bother me overmuch.",shape=box,color=blue];
		87 -> 90;
	88 [label="Firstly, of whose designs are these, \"Necraloids ?\" Of which they are a name and also, perhaps, a designation ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		88 -> 91;
		88 -> 92;
	89 [label="I... do not understand. And how does Loid factor into this ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		89 -> 88;
	90 [label="No, what you might find grotesque in his visage, I assure you, is not the issue I currently have at hand.",shape=box,color=blue];
		90 -> 93;
		90 -> 94;
	91 [label="Your Cardinal Dimanche. Entrati.",shape=box,color=red];
		91 -> 95;
	92 [label="Entrati made that one. But the concept of what they are - Cephalons - was invented by the Orokin.",shape=box,color=red];
		92 -> 95;
	93 [label="I'm surprised the skull isn't off-putting for you.",shape=box,color=red];
		93 -> 96;
	94 [label="I admit, taken out of context, he must be strange. But what in particular is upsetting?",shape=box,color=red];
		94 -> 97;
	95 [label="Excusez-moi, do you mean to imply that le Cardinal made a replicant flying skull servant in the likeness of his own companion, and named them thusly ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		95 -> 98;
	96 [label="You know little of me, which is no fault of yours. I have spent much of my life tending to the dead and the places that they repose. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		96 -> 99;
	97 [label="I find myself curious as to why there is another face upon his back that resembles a child's scrawl.",shape=box,color=blue];
		97 -> 100;
	98 [label="Why are there not more of them, these necraloids, then ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		98 -> 101;
		98 -> 102;
		98 -> 103;
	99 [label="Indeed I have spent much of my life with them as my boon companions. They are keen to listen to my troubles of the day.",shape=box,color=blue];
		99 -> 104;
	100 [label="I inquired with Monsieur Necraloid and Monsieur Loid both, and neither wished to speak of it, they only told me a name. Otak. And it was with great sadness that they uttered it.",shape=box,color=blue];
		100 -> 105;
	101 [label="Maybe he realized how horrifying it is to make yourself a digital copy of your lover.",shape=box,color=red];
		101 -> 106;
	102 [label="Maybe he only ever intended to make the one.",shape=box,color=red];
		102 -> 107;
	103 [label="I'm not sure. Maybe he never got around to making more?",shape=box,color=red];
		103 -> 108;
	104 [label="Update boolean MarieGraveyard1",color=orange];
		104 -> 109;
		104 -> 110;
	105 [label="So here I am, speaking with you, in hopes you might be able to aid me.",shape=box,color=blue];
		105 -> 111;
		105 -> 112;
	106 [label="Ou bien, a tribute to his love and respect, that he did not think this strange laboratory could continue to function without Monsieur Loid.",shape=box,color=blue];
		106 -> 113;
		106 -> 114;
	107 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		107 -> 115;
	108 [label="Imagine it, a school of flying skulls, all effortlessly and perfectly efficient !",shape=box,color=blue];
		108 -> 114;
		108 -> 116;
	109 [label="Did you like looking after graveyards?",shape=box,color=red];
		109 -> 117;
	110 [label="Did they ever respond?",shape=box,color=red];
		110 -> 118;
	111 [label="Do you want to know about Otak? Or why you can't talk to him?",shape=box,color=red];
		111 -> 119;
	112 [label="Otak is hard to explain...",shape=box,color=red];
		112 -> 2918;
	113 [label="I would say that it makes for a strange kind of romantic gesture, but I'm hardly one to talk.",shape=box,color=red];
		113 -> 122;
	114 [label="I wouldn't mind a necraloid buzzing around my place, honestly.",shape=box,color=red];
		114 -> 123;
	115 [label="Tragic and beautiful, in its way, non ? A tribute to his love and respect, that he did not think this strange laboratory could continue to function without Monsieur Loid.",shape=box,color=blue];
		115 -> 124;
		115 -> 113;
	116 [label="I'm glad there's only one of him, honestly. I don't think the world would be ready for that.",shape=box,color=red];
		116 -> 125;
	117 [label="And mausoleums and cryptes, oh yes. But I do admit I preferred the outdoor spaces, though they were challenging for my chair to navigate. No more so than stairs, I fear.",shape=box,color=blue];
		117 -> 126;
	118 [label="Hah ! No, thankfully. Not until your \"Necraloid\" with such a morbid visage replied to me. If speaking to the dead is within the gifts of the Luminaries to bestow, it is not within my knowing.",shape=box,color=blue];
		118 -> 127;
	119 [label="I believe I wish to know both, in time, but I will let you decide where to begin. I do not know which is more important, après tout.",shape=box,color=blue];
		119 -> 2918;
	2918 [label="Check boolean LoidFamilyComplete",color=orange];
		2918 -> 121 [label=true,color=green];
		2918 -> 121 [label=false,color=brown];
		2918 -> 120 [label=false,color=brown];
	122 [label="And now I am intrigued, but that seems a story for another time. Cela dit...",shape=box,color=blue];
		122 -> 97;
	123 [label="Then I have all certainty that you are likely beset by either a need for company or organization, or both. But that is a conversation for another time.",shape=box,color=blue];
		123 -> 97;
	124 [label="I think it had more to do with ensuring this place didn't fall apart at the seams, than anything else.",shape=box,color=red];
		124 -> 130;
	125 [label="Indeed ! As am I. Which brings me to my next question.",shape=box,color=blue];
		125 -> 97;
	126 [label="Update boolean MarieSerum1",color=orange];
		126 -> 131;
		126 -> 132;
	127 [label="No, hearing spirits and voices is much more within the purview of my dear Lyon than I. Though I wonder if Monsieur Necraloid is not haunted as well, judging by the child's scrawl upon the back of his head.",shape=box,color=blue];
		127 -> 133;
	121 [label="Otak used to be an Archimedean, an Orokin scientist and academic. What's happened to him isn't exactly the happiest story.",shape=box,color=red];
		121 -> 129;
	120 [label="Well... in short, some of Entrati's family is upstairs, and they aren't... exactly aware that we're down here.",shape=box,color=red];
		120 -> 128;
	130 [label="And you very well may be right. The flying amalgam seems to be missing much of the real Monsieur Loid's raison d'être and nuance. Cela dit...",shape=box,color=blue];
		130 -> 97;
	131 [label="I didn't know if it was appropriate to ask about whether or not your feet were changed by the serum...",shape=box,color=red];
		131 -> 136;
	132 [label="Your chair?",shape=box,color=red];
		132 -> 137;
	133 [label="That is actually why I came here to speak to you, if you do not mind.",shape=box,color=blue];
		133 -> 100;
	129 [label="Update boolean MarieOtak1",color=orange];
		129 -> 135;
	128 [label="Update boolean MarieFamily1",color=orange];
		128 -> 134;
	136 [label="+10 Chemistry",color=orange];
		136 -> 140;
	137 [label="I do not know what you would name it ? Un fauteuil roulant, or... perhaps a term I deeply dislike, un fauteuil pour invalide.",shape=box,color=blue];
		137 -> 141;
	135 [label="Par les Luminaires... please, go on.",shape=box,color=blue];
		135 -> 139;
	134 [label="Par les Luminaires... You mean that we are all down here in secret ?! Is that why we are not allowed to leave this place ?! Mais pourquoi ?!",shape=box,color=blue];
		134 -> 138;
	140 [label="Oh ! Oh, you poor thing. Imagine you, sitting there, wondering if I had mes pieds taken from me by le Cardinal ! Non, non, non - nothing of the sort.",shape=box,color=blue];
		140 -> 144;
	141 [label="Like what we perch in now, to sit at these little adorable devices to communicate. But with wheels upon the sides, to traverse. A chair with wheels, if you will.",shape=box,color=blue];
		141 -> 145;
		141 -> 146;
	139 [label="By all accounts he was a genius, and the mind behind the harnessing of argon crystals.",shape=box,color=red];
		139 -> 143;
	138 [label="His daughter, Euleria - known as Mother, and her family, have been taking care of Deimos this whole time.",shape=box,color=red];
		138 -> 142;
	144 [label="Sol saw fit to place in my life the inconvenience of having been born with traditionally unwieldy feet. I could not walk. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		144 -> 149;
	145 [label="You were an invalid before you became a protoframe?",shape=box,color=red];
		145 -> 150;
	146 [label="We call them wheelchairs, believe it or not.",shape=box,color=red];
		146 -> 151;
	143 [label="Which are harnessed from the Void - they're the reason we can create a lot of the powerful warframes and weapons we make.",shape=box,color=red];
		143 -> 148;
	142 [label="Watching over this place, and the heart that pumps Void energy into the Origin System, keeping all of us... usable, really, ever since Entrati left.",shape=box,color=red];
		142 -> 861;
	149 [label="But it was simply that, an inconvenience.",shape=box,color=blue];
		149 -> 155;
	150 [label="Non. I very much was not.",shape=box,color=blue];
		150 -> 156;
	151 [label="Hah ! Oh, how I am sitting here laughing at myself for being the fool. Yes, I suppose you would call them wheelchairs, as they are chairs with wheels. Silly me.",shape=box,color=blue];
		151 -> 155;
	148 [label="He specialized in crystallography. And his works were archived here, in the laboratories.",shape=box,color=red];
		148 -> 154;
	861 [label="Check /Lotus/Scripts/1999/DialogueScriptNodes.lua:IsSyndicateRank",color=orange];
		861 -> 152 [label=true,color=green];
		861 -> 153 [label=false,color=brown];
	155 [label="Though, I do not miss having to push myself about. Nor does Lyon, I imagine. What freedom it is to fly !",shape=box,color=blue];
		155 -> 160;
		155 -> 161;
		155 -> 162;
	156 [label="Update boolean MarieInvalid",color=orange];
		156 -> 163;
	154 [label="For some reason, I don't know why, he was turned into a Cephalon, and given his own necraloid shell.",shape=box,color=red];
		154 -> 159;
	152 [label="She's come to terms with his absence, and they've made peace with each other, but it was a hard-won thing.",shape=box,color=red];
		152 -> 157;
	153 [label="She hasn't come to terms with his absence, and they're at each other's throats.",shape=box,color=red];
		153 -> 158;
	160 [label="I try to think of disabilities as things that change us. They limit us in some ways, yes, but they can give us strengths that others don't have.",shape=box,color=red];
		160 -> 167;
	161 [label="You never thought of your condition as a problem?",shape=box,color=red];
		161 -> 168;
	162 [label="Did you know the protoframe serum would do this to you?",shape=box,color=red];
		162 -> 169;
	163 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	159 [label="Not all Cephalons were made as a punishment. But things went... poorly here on Deimos, and he was badly damaged.",shape=box,color=red];
		159 -> 166;
	157 [label="Knowing that he's still out there, running amok, and that he hasn't said a word to her, or even sent a letter...?",shape=box,color=red];
		157 -> 164;
	158 [label="Knowing that he's still out there, running amok, and that he hasn't said a word to her, or even sent a letter...?",shape=box,color=red];
		158 -> 165;
	167 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		167 -> 173;
	168 [label="I never saw the point in bemoaning it. I certainly relish the ability to fetch objects from high shelves without aid, I will tell you that.",shape=box,color=blue];
		168 -> 174;
	169 [label="Oui, le Cardinal told Lyon and I all that would come of taking the sérums that changed our forms. We knew what it would do.",shape=box,color=blue];
		169 -> 175;
	166 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		166 -> 172;
	164 [label="I can't imagine how painful that would be for her. For them.",shape=box,color=red];
		164 -> 170;
	165 [label="It would destroy what little chance of reconciliation they might have.",shape=box,color=red];
		165 -> 171;
	173 [label="Update boolean MarieSecretPower",color=orange];
		173 -> 179;
	174 [label="Ce qui est fait est fait. I could not pray to Sol for a miracle, when so many were hurting more around me, when so many were of greater need. The Luminaries had already given me so much.",shape=box,color=blue];
		174 -> 180;
	175 [label="But like all things, I took mine in joy, and Lyon took his... oh, I fear as if I am telling on him and I should not.",shape=box,color=blue];
		175 -> 181;
		175 -> 182;
	172 [label="Pauvre petit...",shape=box,color=blue];
		172 -> 178;
	170 [label="While I can see the logic behind the decision to protect them from the pain le Cardinal has caused by his necessary departure...",shape=box,color=blue];
		170 -> 176;
	171 [label="+10 Chemistry",color=orange];
		171 -> 177;
	179 [label="Oui ! You understand. I knew the world from another point of view. My arms were stronger. I am more patient. I know what it means to enjoy the moment.",shape=box,color=blue];
		179 -> 190;
	180 [label="I must go. Thank you for this wonderful diversion. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		180 -> 191;
	181 [label="It's all right. Don't tell me anything more than you're comfortable with.",shape=box,color=red];
		181 -> 192;
	182 [label="Please, keep going. I'm having a hard time getting through to him.",shape=box,color=red];
		182 -> 193;
	178 [label="So, he was transferred to the main necraloid - the only Necraloid that remains - and is... well? It's hard to explain.",shape=box,color=red];
		178 -> 187;
		178 -> 188;
		178 -> 189;
	176 [label="I do think it needlessly cruel, don't you ? They might think him dead. Or worse ! And we, living here, comme des rats d'égout ?",shape=box,color=blue];
		176 -> 183;
		176 -> 184;
		176 -> 185;
	177 [label="Oui... I see the logic. I would work to mend their family, if you can, then, non ? It seems to be the only hope any of us have to get out of this place. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		177 -> 186;
	190 [label="When I reach my destination, I bask in the elegance of it. I do not scurry about like a beetle with a billion little legs.",shape=box,color=blue];
		190 -> 202;
	191 [label="Chat ends.",color=orange];
	192 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		192 -> 203;
	193 [label="+5 Chemistry",color=orange];
		193 -> 204;
	187 [label="I just wish we could fix him, honestly. Bring back the real Otak.",shape=box,color=red];
		187 -> 199;
	188 [label="He makes me smile. He's funny, but it hides something tragic and broken.",shape=box,color=red];
		188 -> 200;
	189 [label="Sadly, he's not fixable. And I think he grates on a lot of nerves. ",shape=box,color=red];
		189 -> 201;
	183 [label="You're right. I wish there was something we could do.",shape=box,color=red];
		183 -> 194;
	184 [label="It's not really my decision to make.",shape=box,color=red];
		184 -> 195;
	185 [label="I actually have a friend who loves rats. I think they're adorable.",shape=box,color=red];
		185 -> 196;
	186 [label="Lest we spend the rest of our lives trapped living here, comme des rats d'égout. ",shape=box,color=blue];
		186 -> 197;
		186 -> 198;
	202 [label="I simply wish my dear Lyon could see the world in such a way as you. That all inconveniences may be a secret power, as you say.",shape=box,color=blue];
		202 -> 213;
	203 [label="I appreciate your kindness, Drifter. I will simply leave it at this, as to not overstep any imposition I may be placing upon you - ",shape=box,color=blue];
		203 -> 214;
	204 [label="You are not alone in that, Drifter. Lyon is like family to me, and still sometimes I wonder if I know him any more than the statues of saints in the cathedral.",shape=box,color=blue];
